meta {
  name: monitors
  seq: 2
}

docs {
  Uptime monitor API. A monitor probes one `http://` or `https://` URL every `interval_seconds`
  from the scheduler service, records a heartbeat per probe, and publishes `monitor.up` /
  `monitor.down` when the status flips. Those events reach WebSocket clients and the configured
  notification channels.

  Monitor shape:

  ```json
  {
    "id": "uuid",
    "type": "http",
    "name": "Public website",
    "url": "https://example.com/health",
    "interval_seconds": 60,
    "retries": 1,
    "timeout_seconds": 30,
    "active": true,
    "owner_id": "uuid",
    "cert_expiry_notification": true,
    "domain_expiry_notification": false,
    "max_redirects": 10,
    "save_error_response": false,
    "method": "GET",
    "body_encoding": "json",
    "body": "",
    "headers": { "X-Probe": "nocu" },
    "auth_method": "none",
    "basic_username": "",
    "has_basic_password": false,
    "has_bearer_token": false,
    "last_status": "pending",
    "last_checked_at": null,
    "next_check_at": "...",
    "failure_count": 0,
    "cert_expires_at": null,
    "domain_expires_at": null,
    "notifications": [
      { "id": "uuid", "monitor_id": "uuid", "type": "discord", "enabled": true, "config": { "...": "..." } }
    ],
    "created_at": "...",
    "updated_at": "..."
  }
  ```

  Field groups and rules:

  | Group          | Field                        | Rules                                                      |
  |----------------|------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
  | General        | type                         | `http` only                                                |
  |                | name                         | required                                                   |
  |                | url                          | required, `http` or `https`                                |
  |                | interval_seconds             | default 60, minimum 20                                     |
  |                | retries                      | default 0, consecutive failures tolerated before `down`    |
  |                | timeout_seconds              | default 30, must be lower than `interval_seconds`          |
  | Advanced       | cert_expiry_notification     | publish `monitor.cert_expiring` as the TLS cert nears expiry |
  |                | domain_expiry_notification   | publish `monitor.domain_expiring` as the domain nears expiry |
  |                | max_redirects                | default 10, `0` disables following redirects               |
  |                | save_error_response          | keep the response body of failed probes on the heartbeat   |
  | HTTP options   | method                       | default `GET`; `GET` `POST` `PUT` `PATCH` `DELETE` `HEAD` `OPTIONS` |
  |                | body_encoding                | `json` (default) \| `form` \| `xml`                        |
  |                | body                         | raw request body                                           |
  |                | headers                      | JSON object of string values                               |
  | Authentication | auth_method                  | `none` (default) \| `basic` \| `bearer`                    |
  |                | basic_username / basic_password | required when `basic`                                   |
  |                | bearer_token                 | required when `bearer`                                     |

  Secrets are write-only. Send `basic_password` and `bearer_token` in create or update; responses
  only carry `has_basic_password` and `has_bearer_token`. On `PATCH`, omitting a secret keeps the
  stored value and sending `""` clears it.

  `last_status`: `pending` | `up` | `down`.

  Notification channels (`notifications[].type` and `config`):

  | Type      | Config                                                                                                        |
  |-----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `discord` | `webhook_url` (https `discord.com/api/webhooks/...`), `bot_display_name`, `prefix_custom_message`, `message_format` (`text` default \| `embed`), `disable_url` |
  | `webpush` | `endpoint`, `keys: { p256dh, auth }` — the object returned by `PushSubscription.toJSON()`                     |
  | `webhook` | `post_url`, `http_method` (`POST` default \| `PUT` \| `PATCH`), `request_body` (`json` default \| `form` \| `custom`), `custom_body`, `additional_headers` |

  `custom_body` may use the placeholders `{{monitor_name}}`, `{{monitor_url}}`, `{{status}}` and `{{message}}`.
  Unknown config keys are rejected. A `PATCH` that includes `notifications` replaces the whole set.

  Events:

  | Subject                   | Publisher | Data                                                                  |
  |---------------------------|-----------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `monitor.created`         | core-api  | the monitor                                                           |
  | `monitor.updated`         | core-api  | the monitor                                                           |
  | `monitor.deleted`         | core-api  | `{ "id": "..." }`                                                     |
  | `monitor.up`              | scheduler | `monitor_id, name, url, status, message, http_status, latency_ms, checked_at` (status change only) |
  | `monitor.down`            | scheduler | same as `monitor.up`                                                  |
  | `monitor.cert_expiring`   | scheduler | `monitor_id, name, url, expires_at, days_left` (daily check)          |
  | `monitor.domain_expiring` | scheduler | same as `monitor.cert_expiring`                                       |
}
